{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Real-Virtual Consistency.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Real-Virtual Consistency.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"real virtual consistency real virtual consistency","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Real-Virtual Consistency.md","fileName":"Real-Virtual Consistency.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Real-Virtual Consistency","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-06 21:16\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Augmented Reality Software Architecture]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Augmented Reality Software Architecture","augmentedreality_pearson.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Real-Virtual Consistency.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Real-Virtual Consistency.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"real virtual consistency real virtual consistency","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Real-Virtual Consistency.md","fileName":"Real-Virtual Consistency.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Real-Virtual Consistency","heading":"Real-Virtual Consistency","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Real-virtual consistency is the requirement that software state remain compatible with the physical objects and processes it represents. A real object may move, appear, disappear, or be changed by a person outside the application's control.\n\nThe AR system must sense relevant changes and update virtual behavior without violating expected physical relationships. This consistency extends beyond appearance to interaction, semantics, timing, and the consequences of acting on real objects.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Augmented Reality Software Architecture","augmentedreality_pearson.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Real-Virtual Consistency.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Real-Virtual Consist